WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.914
Kevin, Nadine, and Dad looked at the huge tree lying in their backyard.

2
00:00:12.915 --> 00:00:19.085
"I can't believe the storm blew our tree down," said Nadine.

3
00:00:19.086 --> 00:00:23.016
Tears filled her eyes.

4
00:00:23.017 --> 00:00:28.975
"I loved climbing that tree," Kevin said sadly.

5
00:00:28.976 --> 00:00:33.305
Dad sighed.

6
00:00:33.306 --> 00:00:38.068
"This old oak tree was here when my dad built this house."

7
00:00:38.069 --> 00:00:41.578
A truck pulled into the driveway.

8
00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:45.702
Workers with chainsaws got out.

9
00:00:45.703 --> 00:00:51.233
The workers cut off the small branches.

10
00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:54.554
Then they cut into the thick trunk.

11
00:00:54.555 --> 00:00:57.547
Sawdust filled the air.

12
00:00:57.548 --> 00:01:11.291
With a giant crack, the trunk broke in half.

13
00:01:11.292 --> 00:01:17.049
"It has rings of wood inside!" said Nadine.

14
00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:21.743
"Most trees add one ring every year," said Dad.

15
00:01:21.744 --> 00:01:25.197
"We can count the rings to find the tree's age."

16
00:01:25.198 --> 00:01:43.125
Kevin and Nadine took turns counting.

17
00:01:43.126 --> 00:01:49.486
"Our tree was 213 years old!" Nadine said.

18
00:01:49.487 --> 00:01:55.791
"That's right, and it has a tale to tell," said a lady behind them.

19
00:01:55.792 --> 00:01:59.269
"You must be Dr. Learner," said Dad.

20
00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:03.382
She smiled at the kids.

21
00:02:03.383 --> 00:02:06.763
"Dr. Learner is taking a slab for the Tree Ring Lab.

22
00:02:06.764 --> 00:02:10.916
It's at the University of Arizona," said Dad.

23
00:02:10.917 --> 00:02:17.883
Dr. Learner explained that the Tree Ring Lab had two million tree samples.

24
00:02:17.884 --> 00:02:24.820
"Trees build a picture of the earth's history," she said.

25
00:02:24.821 --> 00:02:28.387
She pointed to a thin ring in the trunk.

26
00:02:28.388 --> 00:02:34.754
"This year had little rain, so your tree did not grow very much."

27
00:02:34.755 --> 00:02:39.540
"Cool!" said Nadine, pointing to a thick ring.

28
00:02:39.541 --> 00:02:42.988
"This year was rainy."

29
00:02:42.989 --> 00:02:47.957
"Trees are like a weather calendar!" said Kevin.

30
00:02:47.958 --> 00:02:51.049
"More than that," said Dr. Learner.

31
00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:54.258
She pointed to a twisted ring.

32
00:02:54.259 --> 00:02:59.570
"This scar shows that something unusual happened—likely a fire.

33
00:02:59.571 --> 00:03:03.115
Trees can tell us about big events.

34
00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:07.386
A tree would grow less if a hurricane blew off its leaves.

35
00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:11.986
Or if a volcano erupted."

36
00:03:11.987 --> 00:03:15.602
Kevin laughed.

37
00:03:15.603 --> 00:03:19.389
"People would remember a volcano eruption!"

38
00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:23.308
Dr. Learner showed them a picture of a tree slab.

39
00:03:23.309 --> 00:03:26.655
It was twice as tall as a man.

40
00:03:26.656 --> 00:03:35.388
"This tree grew from 212 to 1913."

41
00:03:35.389 --> 00:03:43.910
"Whoa! That's 1,701 years!" said Nadine.

42
00:03:43.911 --> 00:03:45.641
Kevin shrugged.

43
00:03:45.642 --> 00:03:51.704
"Okay, maybe trees are better than people at remembering things."

44
00:03:51.705 --> 00:03:55.534
Dr. Learner smiled.

45
00:03:55.535 --> 00:04:00.532
"The oldest living tree is five thousand years old."

46
00:04:00.533 --> 00:04:04.658
Nadine's eyes grew wide.

47
00:04:04.659 --> 00:04:08.849
"How do you know that without cutting it down?"

48
00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:14.390
"We use a tool that drills a tiny hole," said Dr. Learner.

49
00:04:14.391 --> 00:04:23.679
"It doesn't hurt the tree."

50
00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:35.689
The workers finished.

51
00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:37.849
The backyard was quiet.

52
00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:42.317
It looked strange without the tall tree.

53
00:04:42.318 --> 00:04:46.263
Nadine spied something near the fence.

54
00:04:46.264 --> 00:04:52.710
"Look! Our tree had a baby!"

55
00:04:52.711 --> 00:04:55.179
The family hurried over.

56
00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:58.134
The tree was tiny.

57
00:04:58.135 --> 00:05:03.519
"I wonder what stories this tree will tell in the future," said Kevin.

58
00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:07.452
"I don't think you'll find out," said Dad.

59
00:05:07.453 --> 00:05:16.541
"But maybe your grandchildren or your great-grandchildren will."

